# Line-ending policy: LF everywhere in the working tree.
#
# Rationale: hash-pinned artifacts (the frozen evidence bundle) must be
# byte-identical on every platform for `evidence verify` to pass. Git for
# Windows otherwise checks out CRLF, which changes sha256 without changing
# any test-visible behavior — the failure mode is silent until verify runs.
# `text eol=lf` normalizes to LF on commit and checks out LF everywhere;
# token counting is unaffected (the pinned estimator skips whitespace).
* text=auto eol=lf
